  "_comment": [
    "*** NOT A COMPLIANCE REFERENCE. DO NOT COPY THESE STREAM DESCRIPTORS ***",
    "*** INTO A SHIPPING ENTITY MODEL. THEIR LAYOUT IS DELIBERATELY NOT   ***",
    "*** THE ONE THIS PROJECT SHIPS. SEE 'THE TWO LAYOUTS' BELOW.         ***",
    "",
    "AUTHORITATIVE FOR SHIPPING DESCRIPTORS: IEEE 1722.1-2021 Table 7-8",
    "(§7.2.6). formats_offset = 138, redundant_offset = 138+8*N at offset 132,",
    "number_of_redundant_streams at 134, timing at 136, formats at 138, total",
    "138+8*N+2*R. Milan v1.2 §5.3.3.4 requires it: these descriptors 'shall",
    "have the format specified in [ATDECC, Clause 7.2.6]', and Milan v1.2",
    "clause 2 (References) defines [ATDECC] as IEEE Std 1722.1-2021. The",
    "shipping bytes come from avdecc/gen_aem_store.py in the consuming",
    "repository, and its gate 16 (sw/builder/test_builder.py) pins the 138",
    "there. Nothing in THIS file feeds that path: avdecc/gen_aemi_image.py",
    "hands gen_desc_image.py each shipping descriptor as opaque `bytes` sliced",
    "out of gen_aem_store's ROM, never as the `fields` list used here.",
    "",
    "THE TWO LAYOUTS, AND WHY THIS FILE USES THE OTHER ONE. Milan v1.2",
    "Annex C Table C.1 is a second, normative layout: formats_offset = 136,",
    "redundant_offset = 136+8*N, NO timing field, total 136+8*N+2*R. It is",
    "legal for any stream and required for none of ours: §5.3.3.4 says 'A",
    "PAAD-AE may use the extension ... for any of its Streams and shall use it",
    "for the Streams that are part of the redundant pair', and this model",
    "declares no redundant pair (R = 0). This vector uses it BECAUSE it",
    "disagrees with the shipping packer. KL_aecp_desc_store takes every",
    "descriptor length from the index map's `elem_len` and never reads a",
    "descriptor's interior, so image.bin is the one image the RTL suite boots",
    "whose formats_offset contradicts the length its index map declares:",
    "136+8*2 = 152 here, where §7.2.6 would size the same descriptor 154. Code",
    "that starts deriving a length or an offset from a descriptor's interior",
    "fails on the next run of tb/desc_store. Move this file to 138 and every",
    "descriptor the RTL ever sees carries one packer's layout, which is exactly",
    "the agreement-by-coincidence this vector exists to deny.",
    "",
    "The eight-descriptor Milan tree of docs/architecture/07 §3.1 (ENTITY,",
    "CONFIGURATION, AUDIO_UNIT, STREAM_INPUT, STREAM_OUTPUT, AVB_INTERFACE,",
    "CLOCK_SOURCE, CLOCK_DOMAIN), 1 configuration / 1 in / 1 out / 2 formats.",
    "Identity values are deliberately generic: this repository ships no",
    "vendor's entity model; an integrator points the generator at its own.",
    "Lengths land on 07 §3.2: ENTITY 312, CONFIGURATION 74+4*6, AUDIO_UNIT",
    "144+4*2, STREAM_* 136+8*2 (Annex C, above), AVB_INTERFACE 102,",
    "CLOCK_SOURCE 86, CLOCK_DOMAIN 76+2*1. DescriptorImage.MILAN_8 in the",
    "consuming repository's tests/steps/aecp_engine_steps.py models these same",
    "lengths and must move whenever they do."
  ],
